{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KfDXZCrdN9VPzkR8j7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\n**Project Summary**\n\n[Clinic Name] is a two-attorney legal aid clinic that represents tenants facing eviction in [County]. We request $90,000 over two years ($45,000 a year) to fund a staff attorney position.\n\n**Need.** Last year 1,140 eviction cases were filed in [County]. We represented the tenant in 163 of them, about one in seven. We turned away roughly 300 more tenants because no attorney was free. Each of our attorneys carries about 80 open cases, and one of them leaves in June.\n\n**Results.** In the cases we handled last year, 58% ended with the tenant keeping their home or getting at least 60 days to move. We don't yet have a comparable figure for tenants without a lawyer in our county. Starting in January, we will request court-wide outcome data from the county clerk so we can compare our results against it.\n\n**Plan.** We will begin recruiting as soon as the award is announced. Our last attorney search took five months. The new attorney will take cases from tenants we would otherwise turn away.\n\n**Funding.** The position costs $78,000 a year with benefits. Alongside the Foundation's $45,000, a $20,000 annual pledge from [Family Fund] and $13,000 a year from our general budget would cover it, for a two-year total of $156,000. Our $60,000 annual county contract is up for renewal in October.\n\n**Reporting.** Every six months we will report to the Foundation the number of cases the attorney opened and how each one ended. Once the clerk's data is available, we will include the court-wide comparison.\n</final_document>\n\nThis comes to about 240 words. Some notes on what I decided:\n\n- **\"A staff attorney position,\" not \"a third attorney.\"** You don't have a plan to replace the attorney leaving in June. Until you do, this hire may keep you at two lawyers instead of three. The summary mentions the June departure and doesn't promise a third attorney, so it stays true either way. If you secure money to replace her before you submit, change the request line to \"a third staff attorney.\"\n- **I included the county renewal.** It's one sentence, and the foundation will probably see it in your budget anyway. It's better coming from you. Cut it if the application has a separate budget section where it fits better.\n- **What I left out because you don't know it yet:** how many more tenants the new attorney will serve, a start date, and a comparison for the 58%. The six-month reporting and the January data request are there to make up for those gaps with commitments you can actually keep.\n- **Placeholders to fill in:** clinic name, county, and the family fund's name. Check whether the fund is OK with being named.\n- **Check the budget numbers.** $45,000 + $20,000 + $13,000 = $78,000 a year, or $156,000 over two years."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":10190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1017},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"913aafc7-7d98-4da5-8ade-b7b4d17fda90","uuid":"1b757c09-3051-42ad-8c7d-9ca099896bcb","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:33:04.948Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KfDP8btxTeakwbtYLz"}
